# WFORMT.KEY - the main key script of the form dialog's test,
# TEST/WFORMT.C, run by "WIN WFORMT TDATA /KEYS:WFORMT.KEY
# /SNAP:WFORMT.SNP" on the seeded data; every mode of Windows writes
# TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/WFORMT.SNP.  A new item is added and an item changed,
# each shown again as the server holds it; the title's count shows each
# save's busy note.  Then the item form's access letters.
S START
# F2: a new item with its defaults; the focus starts on Category, the
# first field that can be changed.  Maker and Model, above the tabs, by
# their letters; the date and the price on the Acquisition page, which
# CTRL-TAB twice shows.
K F2
S NEW
T CC
K TAB
T D
K TAB
T Video
K ALT-M
T Compaq
K TAB
T Portable
K ALT-L
T b2
K CTRL-TAB CTRL-TAB
T 1984-03-15
K TAB TAB
T 299.95
S TYPED
# OK adds it: the item read again, in view mode, has the ID ADD gave.
K ENTER
S ADDED
K ENTER
S BACK
# F3: the new item in edit mode; its quantity changed, OK sets it, and
# the item read again shows the new quantity.
K F3
S EDIT
K TAB TAB TAB TAB TAB
T 3
K ENTER
S SET
K ENTER
# F4: the same item in view mode, with its Edit button and OK.
K F4
S VIEW
K ESC
# The item form's access letters in edit mode: Condition's code, then
# Price paid and Value, on the Acquisition page.
K F3
K ALT-I
S ALTI
K ALT-P
S ALTP
K ALT-V
S ALTV
K ESC
S DONE
